    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Just Something is the eagerly awaited new album by British soul vocalist Dee C. Lee, released on Acid Jazz Records in 2024, featuring 11 tracks that blend funk, soul, acid jazz, and subtle West Coast influences. Primarily comprising nine originals co-written by Lee herself, alongside covers like Stevie Wonder's \"For Once in My Life\" and an emotive \"I Love You,\" the record showcases her rich, expressive voice over irresistible rhythms, fierce flute trills, and shimmering arrangements that evoke the late '70s and early '80s jazz-funk era. Tracks such as \"Back In Time,\" \"Don't Forget About Love,\" \"Mountains,\" and \"Trojan Horse\" highlight her knack for crafting funky, uplifting grooves that pivot seamlessly from introspection to self-assured joy, backed by collaborators including Matt Berry, The Brand New Heavies, and Billy Valentine.\n\nDrawing from Lee's storied career—spanning her time with Wham!, The Style Council, and reunions like the 2019 documentary-inspired re-recording of \"The Long Hot Summer\"—Just Something feels like a triumphant return, not mere retro nostalgia but a vivid sonic time capsule that sounds authentically of its inspirational period. Critics praise its depth, with soulful standouts like \"How To Love\" and \"Every Day Summer\" underscoring themes of cherishing memories, embracing love, and personal empowerment, culminating in a dedication to live music, mutual love, and peace. Available on signed LP and CD via Acid Jazz, the album's polished production and Lee's commanding presence mark it as a significant milestone in her discography, bridging her past legacies with contemporary vibrancy.",
